  "he:Third Meal/Motzaei Shabbat Prayers:10": {
   "kind": "commentary",
   "en": "Rabbi Yochanan said: In every place where you find the greatness of the Holy One, blessed be He, there you find His humility. This is written in the Torah, taught in the Prophets, and repeated three times in the Writings."
  },
  "he:Third Meal/Motzaei Shabbat Prayers:11": {
   "kind": "commentary",
   "en": "Written in the Torah: For the Lord your God is the God of gods and the Lord of lords, the great, mighty, and awesome God who shows no partiality and takes no bribe. And it is written immediately after: He executes justice for the orphan and the widow, and loves the stranger, giving him food and clothing. Taught in the Prophets: For thus says the High and Lofty One who dwells in eternity, whose name is Holy: I dwell in the high and holy place, and also with the contrite and lowly of spirit, to revive the spirit of the lowly and to revive the heart of the contrite. Repeated three times in the Writings: Sing to God, sing praises to His name; extol Him who rides upon the clouds; His name is the Lord, and rejoice before Him. And it is written immediately after: A father of orphans and a defender of widows is God in His holy dwelling. May the Lord our God be with us as He was with our fathers; may He not forsake us and may He not abandon us. And you who cling to the Lord your God are alive, all of you, today. For the Lord will comfort Zion; He will comfort all her ruins, and will make her wilderness like Eden, and her desert like the garden of the Lord; joy and gladness will be found in her, thanksgiving and the voice of song. For the Lord's sake He will magnify the Torah and glorify it."
  },
